WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:06.798 --> 00:00:11.848
People with disabilities are somehow
always different.

00:00:12.733 --> 00:00:17.105
Wherever we are, we are changing
something in the world.

00:00:18.040 --> 00:00:28.223
I'm at the moment where I'm trying
to confront viewers with how I live

00:00:28.223 --> 00:00:32.277
with a disability and a non-normative body.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.945
Society tells you what to do.

00:00:35.945 --> 00:00:38.758
How you should move,
how you should pick a glass of water.

00:00:38.758 --> 00:00:43.752
And if something goes away
from the norm, it's very weird.

00:00:43.752 --> 00:00:46.555
People don't know how to react to that.

00:00:47.442 --> 00:00:50.800
Disabled bodies in public spaces
is making a political statement,

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:53.212
whether they're doing anything
or not.

00:00:53.212 --> 00:01:01.552
I always have insisted on the need
for disabled artists

00:01:01.552 --> 00:01:06.792
or artists with learning difficulties

00:01:06.792 --> 00:01:12.435
to take charge of those positions

00:01:12.435 --> 00:01:19.625
like directing, teaching,
curating, programming,

00:01:19.625 --> 00:01:24.200
producing, initiating,

00:01:24.200 --> 00:01:28.640
and in that sense

00:01:28.640 --> 00:01:34.598
it's happening a lot.

00:01:36.515 --> 00:01:40.103
Each disabled artist has
a different set of needs

00:01:40.103 --> 00:01:44.432
but I believe that the goal of art
is to create change.

00:01:45.203 --> 00:01:49.680
For me creating, moving, dancing

00:01:49.680 --> 00:01:53.698
is a sense of freedom
and independence

00:01:53.698 --> 00:01:58.795
but also a form of opposition and resistance,
a form of shouting and anger.

